{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539674-a-good-totem-for-a-caern-of-crafting","id":1539674,"title":"A good totem for a Caern of Crafting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-01T19:37:27-07:00","id":1539674,"title":"A good totem for a Caern of Crafting?","content":"Besides Fire Drake, are there any particularly good Caerns of Craftsmanship totems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T23:17:50-07:00","id":1539680,"title":"","content":"My answer is not based on canon because I think WtA sourcebooks often fail at providing good examples of caern and pack totems. So I will answer according to what I think would be good answers (meaning not necessarily supported by canon examples).<br /> <br /> A totem of craftsmanship basically means a spirit whose material correspondent makes or uses tools. There are not many animals that do so, but there are enough to give you a good selection.<br /> <br /> Beaver (actually a pack totem found in some sourcebooks)<br /> Crows (and other corvids) - there are many such canonical totems, but none that directly deal with their using of tools<br /> Elephants - again there is a canonical elephant totem, but it does not deal with their tool use<br /> Octopus - probably too strange to be a Garou totem<br /> Sea Otters - another canonical totem, but again it does not involve the otters use of tools<br /> Ants - for some reason ants have never been used as a totem<br /> Various Primates<br /> <br /> If I was to decide which one was best, I'd probably pick Beaver. I think technically they don't use tools, but they obviously build things and that counts towards craftsmanship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T01:32:20-07:00","id":1539683,"title":"","content":"You can also look for animals with a &quot;building&quot; thematics, beaver have already been names, but Spiders could be a good fit, and you could link it to the Ananasi, like a social bonus.<br /> Gallia (from the white howler book) could be a good fit, as well, though it would mean she didn't fall.<br /> Brigid feels like a very good candidate to me you could just adapt her to fit the local god of creativity (artists/craftmanship)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T03:06:33-07:00","id":1539685,"title":"","content":"Hakahe, the Incarna of the planet Vulcan who represents secrecy, darkness and silence is a good choice<br /> Among other names, he is called Khnemu, Goibnu, Volundr, Tehuti.and <b>Hephaestus</b><br /> He favors the Uktena, smiths and crafters.<br /> The qualities of both creation and destruction fall under the province of the Ebon Whisperer, reminding those that in order to make something new, we often need to break what has gone before.<br /> Hakahe grants additional three dice on Crafts and Repair rolls, and teaches his children the Gift: Reshape Object. All Occult rolls made by his Childre are at -2 difficulty. - ideal for crafters and anything spiritual and occult realted to that<br /> His ban is an interesting one, Children of Hakahe must work to build things importance among human communities, the better to teach humans to build rather than destroy.<br /> <br /> He is from WTA: Rage Across the Heavens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T08:47:59-07:00","id":1539700,"title":"","content":"What about Cockroach? In real life, cockroaches don\u2019t actually build anything, but the spirit parent of cockroach seems to be all about technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T09:09:17-07:00","id":1539702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539674-a-good-totem-for-a-caern-of-crafting?p=1539700#post1539700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Cockroach? In real life, cockroaches don\u2019t actually build anything, but the spirit parent of cockroach seems to be all about technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cockroach is more about survival and adapting. It is technology -now- because that's what rules the world. But in the past it has been religion, merchants and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T09:11:24-07:00","id":1539703,"title":"","content":"Shantar is the incarna of creativity and inventiveness. One of her avatars could definitely be a patron to a caern of crafting, so long as you don't mind the tentacles and are polite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T11:45:10-07:00","id":1539716,"title":"","content":"Shantar and Hakahe both sound like really good choices. So does Beaver and Spider. Thank you all, and I would love to hear any other suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T13:08:33-07:00","id":1539719,"title":"","content":"Beaver, Spider, Monkey &amp; Otter are all good pulls imo, those are also where my mind went.<br /> <br /> Bee perhaps could also fit, although that\u2019s a bit more architecture and community then tool-use.<br /> <br /> Is there any other details about the particular Caern you can share that might help with nailing down a spirit with thematic resonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T16:15:55-07:00","id":1539725,"title":"","content":"Those that Directly add to Crafts are Firedrake, Beaver, Brighid, General Lee ( maybe a reskin on this one), Hakahe, Shantar and probably a couple I'm missing from outlying books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T09:20:02-07:00","id":1539753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539674-a-good-totem-for-a-caern-of-crafting?p=1539719#post1539719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beaver, Spider, Monkey &amp; Otter are all good pulls imo, those are also where my mind went.<br /> <br /> Bee perhaps could also fit, although that\u2019s a bit more architecture and community then tool-use.<br /> <br /> Is there any other details about the particular Caern you can share that might help with nailing down a spirit with thematic resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking of a hill that is somewhere rural, with a series of small smithies nested with in. But possibly also with a new and larger and more high tech laboratory that the Glass Walkers created, and is geared towards building things that are more technological.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T14:39:14-07:00","id":1539766,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the natural resources to be found there include things like ochre and other natural earth pigments, metal impregnated sands, vividly colored coats, semi precious stones, wood with unusual grain patterns, and hard to find plant dyes make this a spot that artisans of all walks naturally gravitate toward? I know of art collectives that will acquire pieces of land for exactly this purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T13:03:01-07:00","id":1539800,"title":"","content":"I would consider not over-thinking this too much. Caern/Sept spirits are much more flavor than mechanics. A Sept can only call on their protector once a month, and usually the bonuses only last one night (or one intense combat scene). A single night of crafting bonuses a month is not going to justify (by itself) a Sept that's a hub of workshops, smithies, and so on. The flavor is going to matter a lot more. Spirits like Cockroach, Termite, or Paper Wasp (I don't think Paper Wasp ever got its own full Totem write up, but Caern ones are easier to home brew), are more likely to encourage a Sept to build in a hive style around the Caern with lots of specialized spaces around it. Danu, Brigid, or the Muses (stat-wise not the best for general crafting, but art is good enough for the example) are all more encouraging of both individual interests and some crafts you don't necessarily want crowded all in one place (lots of traditional crafts were performed at the edges of settlements for a number of reasons, the smell particularly).<br /> <br /> If you're really stuck between two spirits (and you're even bothering with the expanded Caern rules like in W20 Rage Across the World were it matters), let the mechanics decide... but otherwise focus on the flavor of the spirit and how that impacts how the Garou there live to be in harmony with that spiritual impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}